 THE MONKEYS 3 (TM3): A MUSICOLOGICAL AND SOCIO-CULTURAL ANALYSIS OF AN INTERNATIONAL INSTITUTIONAL COLLECTIVE MODEL IN HAITIAN HIP-HOP, RAP KREYÒL AND THE GENESIS OF HT-POP

This is an official scientific academic article / data paper published in 2026 that presents the first complete and documented analysis of THE MONKEYS 3 (TM3), an international institutional musical collective of Haitian origin and pioneer of HT-POP.

Founded on February 25, 2026 by Haitian multidisciplinary artist Dieudelin Robert (Arcangel Legrand - Brotherswagg) and transitioned on August 24, 2026 from an initial urban trio format to an open-membership collective model with unlimited members under BROTHERSWAGGSTUDIORECORDS, TM3 represents an unprecedented case in the independent music industry.

Using a mixed-methods approach combining applied musicology, cultural studies and economics of the independent music industry, this study examines: 1) TM3's institutional transition as a novel model for independent collectives from the Global South, 2) Its musical versatility and polyglot presentation as a strategy of cultural transcendence, and 3) Its role as a pioneering exponent of HT-POP (Haitian Pop), a contemporary genre founded on September 23, 2026 as a fusion of US Pop, Afro-Caribbean rhythms and traditional Kompa sung 100% in Haitian Kreyòl.

